{"seq":3,"slug":"rust-language","title":"Rust 语言","stage":"DONE","category":"languages","chapterCount":5,"docCount":20,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/rust-language","rating":{"composite":3.71,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":4.2,"coverage":3.75,"positioning":3,"strategic":3.67},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":{"composite":3.11,"verdict":"skip-for-this-profile","uScore":1.5}},"introMarkdown":"# Rust 语言 简介\n\nRust 是一门专注于安全性、并发性和高性能的系统级编程语言。它通过独创的所有权系统在编译期消除了数据竞争和内存安全问题，无需垃圾回收器即可实现内存的自动管理。自诞生以来，Rust 连续多年被开发者评为最受喜爱的编程语言，并在操作系统、WebAssembly、嵌入式开发、网络服务等领域得到广泛应用。\n\n本手册面向具有其他编程语言经验、希望学习 Rust 的软件开发者，以及对系统编程感兴趣的技术爱好者。无论你来自 C/C++、Go、Python 还是 JavaScript 背景，都能在这里找到清晰的学习路径。\n\n全书将覆盖以下核心主题：Rust 基础语法与类型系统、所有权与借用机制、生命周期的理解与应用、结构体与枚举的模式匹配、trait 系统与泛型编程、错误处理策略、并发编程模型、unsafe Rust 与 FFI 接口，以及 Cargo 生态与项目工程化实践。通过系统学习，你将掌握用 Rust 编写安全且高效程序的能力。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"ownership-and-borrowing","title":"所有权与借用","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/rust-language/ownership-and-borrowing","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"ownership-rules","title":"所有权规则与移动语义","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/rust-language/ownership-and-borrowing/ownership-rules"},{"seq":2,"slug":"references-and-borrowing","title":"引用与借用规则","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/rust-language/ownership-and-borrowing/references-and-borrowing"},{"seq":3,"slug":"lifetimes","title":"生命周期标注","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/rust-language/ownership-and-borrowing/lifetimes"},{"seq":4,"slug":"smart-pointers","title":"智能指针","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/rust-language/ownership-and-borrowing/smart-pointers"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"type-system","title":"类型系统","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/rust-language/type-system","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"traits-and-generics","title":"Trait 与泛型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/rust-language/type-system/traits-and-generics"},{"seq":2,"slug":"enums-and-pattern-matching","title":"枚举与模式匹配","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/rust-language/ty